{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghijgobQYsd9e9rkzwzi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The faked-gamepad run passes all 6 checks: ✕ runs the rail, the glyphs are the DualSense's (✕), L2 aims, the right stick turns the view, R2 fires, and there are no page errors.\n\nThe feature-completeness question is about what counts as a TASK.md feature, so here is my reading. TASK.md says that where it and the plan disagree, TASK.md wins. The items I cut (the Palais, the glacier archive, the oompah-band boss, the slalom duel) come from PLAN.md, not TASK.md. Every feature TASK.md lists is built and was exercised:\n\n| TASK.md feature | Where it was checked |\n|---|---|\n| Feature-complete vertical slice: rails, scan, Warm Spot shooting, seven coats and skills, Wax Bench, Wardrobe, Sweep, gates, two bosses, results, saves | Bot playthrough from a new game to the credits, in Node and in the real page |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, with live sliders and reset to defaults | Browser screenshots; Node slider checks |\n| Attract mode (starts after 10 s idle, any input exits) | Browser run: it started at exactly 10.0 s, and a key press returned to the title |\n| AI Hub multiplayer (ghost-mode Echo Run) | Hub harness: 2 players, and 4 players under latency, jitter and loss, including host-leave |\n| 10-foot controller-first UI, PlayStation glyphs by default with an Xbox option, key and mouse glyphs | Glyph screenshots; the new faked-gamepad test |\n| Touch-only notice | Browser run with a touch-only phone profile |\n| Source Information and feedback sections in chat and in the in-game About screen | Both present |\n| No TODOs or placeholders | The build fails if the bundle contains any |\n\nI have not tested pointer-lock mouse aim. The engine's mouse-capture path can't be driven headless, and I added a pointer-offset fallback for when the mouse isn't captured. That is the one input path left unverified.\n\nThe final deliverables are unchanged:\n- `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-023141.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`, which parses and answers every field\n- The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections in my previous reply, which are also in the in-game About screen\n\nI added `tests/browser/pad.mjs`; `node tests/run.mjs --browser` does not include it yet, so run it directly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":261,"cache_read_input_tokens":493635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":261},"output_tokens":768,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72551944-ea0f-4259-bd61-d1afd3ec3816","uuid":"4957ef6d-15d0-48bb-bf22-f43e08730da9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:21:05.302Z","request_id":"req_011CghijgLJZxk19HgX1quU1"}
