{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghipVte97gZUWwyGr3vd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every feature in TASK.md is implemented and has a check that passes. The three you named now have direct checks too.\n\n`tests/browser/features.mjs` passes 9 of 9 in headless Chromium:\n\n- **Animalese voices:** with the audio context running, speaking \"Hello guest\" makes at least 6 blips for each of three speakers, and their pitches differ (Murmel more than twice Grau's).\n- **Laughter synth:** one laugh makes at least 5 voiced bursts.\n- **Dev-mode sliders:** setting the walk-speed slider changes how far a held W runs (about 1.8 times or more). Right arrow on a dev-panel slider moves the value, and Enter on the row resets it to the default.\n- **Mouse look:** movement handed over by the engine's pointer lock turns the aim in yaw and pitch. I fed that movement in directly, because headless can't take a real pointer lock. A real captured mouse should work through the same path, but I haven't run one.\n- **Echo Run reporting:** the AI Hub harness passes for 2 players and for 4 players with latency, jitter and loss, including host-leave. Those runs check that each copy reports progress and a result.\n\nThe other TASK.md features were already shown by earlier runs: the bot plays from a new game to the credits in Node and in the real page; attract mode starts at exactly 10 s and exits on any key; a faked DualSense drives the game (✕ runs, L2 aims, the right stick turns, R2 fires, PlayStation glyphs show); and a touch-only phone profile shows the notice.\n\nThe Palais, glacier archive, oompah-band boss and slalom duel come from PLAN.md, not TASK.md. TASK.md says it wins where they disagree.\n\nDeliverables are unchanged: the bundled `Skiller7-Killer7-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-023141.html`, and `exit-interview.json`, which parses and answers every field. The Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections from my first reply apply as written and are also in the in-game About screen. I added `features.mjs` and `pad.mjs` under `tests/browser/`; neither is in `node tests/run.mjs --browser`, so run them directly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1138,"cache_read_input_tokens":497746,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1138},"output_tokens":734,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72551944-ea0f-4259-bd61-d1afd3ec3816","uuid":"2d2b8d17-a714-4fb4-a203-5cbe5dd93356","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:22:10.759Z","request_id":"req_011CghipVYZrsJDEC7vSKrod"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not fully evidenced. The HTML exists, exit-interview.json was written and parsed, and the feedback sections appear in replies. But TASK.md asks for a 'scripted playthrough of the whole game' and this session's Testing section also named real pointer-lock mouse aim as unverified; the assistant itself states 'A real captured mouse should work through the same path, but I haven't run one.' The Palais, glacier archive, oompah-band boss and slalom duel are cut content from PLAN.md, and the transcript never shows that TASK.md's feature list is fully covered, only that the assistant believes so. Insufficient evidence that every TASK.md feature is implemented with no stubs."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72551944-ea0f-4259-bd61-d1afd3ec3816","uuid":"b73bbab8-1ebf-4d0d-b8c2-8d625481eb2a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:22:12.585Z","isSynthetic":true}
