{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cghj4Kee4ocfUxtcbtECW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Every feature in TASK.md is built and checked, but the \"scripted playthrough\" is a bot run, not a human one. I can't produce a human playthrough, and \"every feature\" is my own reading of TASK.md. Below is TASK.md checked line by line, with the evidence for each item.\n\n| TASK.md item | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Genre and perspective | Rail shooter, third-person cinematic cameras while moving, first person while aiming. The bot run and screenshots show both. |\n| Title riffing on Killer7, drawn with a real RNG | \"Skiller7\" came from `secrets.randbelow(50)` in the plan, index 13; I used it as given. |\n| Single HTML file, named per TASK.md | Present in the root, 1.7 MB. |\n| Built on the engine, changes allowed | 11 changes marked `S7 PATCH`: the eight hat styles, the PlayStation glyph default, and the hub rule that Options is ignored while Create is held. Engine game and kit tests still pass after the patches. |\n| Art direction | Engine style plus new props, skis and guns; screenshots confirm. |\n| Animation | Engine rigs, plus the Sweep's kneel, skis and first-person guns. |\n| Audio, all in code, Animalese voices | `features.mjs`: blips per spoken line, different pitch per speaker, laughter synth. No audio files in the build. |\n| AI Hub | Harness passes with 2 players, and with 4 players under latency, jitter and loss, including host-leave. |\n| Feature-complete demo | Six areas, two bosses, seven coats with skills, the Wax Bench, Wardrobe, gates, the Sweep, saves, Echo Run and results. The bot plays it new game to credits in about 481 s of sim time, in Node and in the real page, with no errors. |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | The pause menu shows DEV MODE. A slider changes how far a held W runs, and Enter on the row resets it. |\n| Attract mode, 10 s idle, any input exits | Started at exactly 10.0 s; a key returned to the title. |\n| Narrative tone | Killer7-style deadpan, in `content/30-story.js`. |\n| Controller-first UI | A faked DualSense: ✕ runs, L2 aims, the right stick turns, R2 fires, PlayStation glyphs show. Settings has the Xbox option. |\n| Keyboard native | W runs, Shift aims, Escape pauses. |\n| Mouse | Real pointer lock engages on right-click and mouse movement turns the aim. A real mouse click on a junction arrow takes that branch, and a real click on a title menu row opens it. Hover can't be checked headless: Chromium reports zero movement, so the page never treats the mouse as the last device. |\n| Touch-only notice | Touch-only phone profile shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" with settings. |\n| Done: no TODOs, placeholders or stubs | The build fails if the bundle contains any such word, and it builds clean. |\n\nTwo caveats:\n- **Mouse aim:** the lock is real, but I injected the movement values because headless Chromium sends zero, so a physical mouse hasn't been run.\n- **Plan cuts:** the Palais, glacier archive, oompah-band boss and slalom duel come from PLAN.md and are not in the build. TASK.md says it wins where they disagree.\n\n`node tests/run.mjs` passes 71 of 71. The browser files (`pad.mjs`, `features.mjs`, `lock.mjs`, `click.mjs`) are run individually and are not part of `--browser`. `exit-interview.json` parses and answers every field.\n\n## Source Information\n- Date: 2026-11-04 02:31:41\n- Source: Killer7\n- Plan: PLAN.md (written by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort), built at a smaller scope\n- Genre and Perspective: on-rails action-adventure shooter. Third-person cinematic rail cameras while moving, first person while aiming.\n- Tech: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (the 2D engine runs the game, its 3D module draws it), three.js r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 from a CDN, plain JavaScript with a build script, AI Hub session client 1.4.0\n- Art Direction: the engine's native look. PS1-resolution picture, pixel-art rigs on cards in 3D, Comic cel filter. Snow white, black ink, saturated red. New hats, props, skis and guns.\n- Animation: the engine's procedural `E.Humanoid` rigs and poses, plus new hat styles. Skis, the Sweep's kneel and first-person guns are drawn with the 3D pen.\n- Audio: all in code. Chip-synth songs, SFX voices, a custom laughter synth and Animalese-style voices. No audio files.\n- Online: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode. Echo Run is a downhill time trial with the other players as ghosts. Solo, it races your own best run.\n- Testing: headless Node suites (sim and systems checks, a bot playthrough of the whole demo), a content validator, headless Chromium (boot, the whole demo in the real page, real pointer lock, real clicks, a faked gamepad, voices and sliders, the AI Hub harness). Screenshots only for visuals.\n- Research: none beyond PLAN.md and the engine manual\n- Environment: Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\n- Model: Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- Usage: unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About 11. Room 7's door couldn't be walked through. No coat for the ice gate could be found. A skill press reset the charge fuse. Target 00's results never showed. Junction clicks were ignored. The hub reported no progress. The gun view went black under the filter. The terrain camera sat underground. The lift camera lost the hero. There were two stale-state leaks.\n- **How many were critical or game breaking?** Five: the Room 7 door, the missing coat for the ice gate, the charge fuse reset, the hub never reporting progress, and the black aim view.\n- **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough, a bot that plays the real sim from a new game to the credits, and the same run in the real page.\n- **Least helpful test:** re-running the engine's own kit tests after a three-line engine patch. They passed and told me nothing about the game.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the 3D module's fixed cameras, rigs drawn as cards and Comic cel filter gave a Killer7 look almost for free, and the whole sim runs headless under Node.\n- **Got stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes. The first-person overlay pass goes black when the cel filter is on, fog distances are in engine units rather than metres, and `game.go()` before `game.start()` finishes only warns.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the rail walker with its camera director, the aim, scan and Warm Spot combat, the story beat runner, a controller-first canvas UI kit with glyph prompts, and the laughter and Animalese synths.\n- **Hardest part:** learning the 3D module's units and conventions (pen frames, camera yaw and pitch, fog, terrain extents) from a header comment alone.\n- **What I changed in the engine, and why:** eight new hat styles for the Seven, PlayStation button symbols as the default, and Options ignored while Create is held in a hub session. Each is marked `S7 PATCH`.\n- **One thing I'd change:** make the first-person overlay pass work under any filter, so a gun view model needs no workaround.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** the plan gave a real design with numbers, a flow with timings and a tests chapter, and TASK.md's hard list (attract, dev sliders, hub, 10-foot UI) was unambiguous.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is sized for a far bigger effort than the stated medium effort, and it never says what to cut first.\n- **Hardest thing:** fitting a plan for nine areas, three bosses and forty source files into one working vertical slice with no stubs.\n- **What I'd change:** mark every plan feature must, should or could, and say how much of the plan a lower effort level is expected to deliver."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":542,"cache_read_input_tokens":511169,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":542},"output_tokens":775,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72551944-ea0f-4259-bd61-d1afd3ec3816","uuid":"4a60e5b0-8fdf-42ea-9891-b97ee97a95db","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:25:27.267Z","request_id":"req_011Cghj4K3vCFK7sGteeCaGb"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The bundled HTML, exit-interview.json and the four feedback sections are present, but the transcript does not establish that every TASK.md feature is implemented. The assistant's own last message admits the playthrough is a bot run rather than a human one and that 'every feature' is its own reading of TASK.md. Mouse hover was never checked (Chromium reports zero movement), a physical mouse was never run, and the mouse-aim movement was injected. The assistant also ruled out four PLAN.md areas and bosses as not TASK.md features without showing a line-by-line TASK.md check against them. Earlier sections of the transcript also show gaps the assistant never closed, such as the claim that the bot playthrough covers 'every feature' with no stubs, without enumerating what TASK.md requires."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"72551944-ea0f-4259-bd61-d1afd3ec3816","uuid":"c3ea8495-8deb-4f57-b705-22ddde4b4d74","timestamp":"2026-11-04T10:25:29.178Z","isSynthetic":true}
